      "title": "Deforestation",
      "type": "FIB_R",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Deforestation can disrupt the lives of local communities, sometimes with <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"facilities\">facilities</option><option value=\"benign\">benign</option><option value=\"resources\">resources</option><option value=\"off\">off</option><option value=\"apart\">apart</option><option value=\"devastating\">devastating</option><option value=\"prerequisites\">prerequisites</option><option value=\"consequences\">consequences</option></select> consequences . Forests provide a vast array of <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"facilities\">facilities</option><option value=\"benign\">benign</option><option value=\"resources\">resources</option><option value=\"off\">off</option><option value=\"apart\">apart</option><option value=\"devastating\">devastating</option><option value=\"prerequisites\">prerequisites</option><option value=\"consequences\">consequences</option></select> to all of us, including food, wood, medicine, fresh water, and the air we breathe. Without the trees, species can disappear, the natural water balance can become disrupted and the ecosystem that supports the human population can fall <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"facilities\">facilities</option><option value=\"benign\">benign</option><option value=\"resources\">resources</option><option value=\"off\">off</option><option value=\"apart\">apart</option><option value=\"devastating\">devastating</option><option value=\"prerequisites\">prerequisites</option><option value=\"consequences\">consequences</option></select> .</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、devastating</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“with ______ consequences”，devastating consequences 是常见搭配，意为“毁灭性的后果”。表示森林砍伐会破坏当地社区的生活，有时会带来毁灭性的后果。因此填 devastating。</p>\n<p>2、resources</p>\n<p>考点:上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“a vast array of ______ to all of us”，后文列举了 food、wood、medicine、fresh water 和 air，这些都是森林提供的“资源”。resources 意为“资源”，与后文的列举内容语义一致。因此填 resources。</p>\n<p>3、apart</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“fall ______”，fall apart 是固定搭配，意为“崩溃/瓦解”。表示支撑人类人口的生态系统可能会崩溃。因此填 apart。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Deforestation can disrupt the lives of local communities, sometimes with devastating consequences。</p>\n<p>森林砍伐可能会破坏当地社区的生活,有时会带来毁灭性的后果。</p>\n<p>Forests provide a vast array of resources to all of us, including food, wood, medicine, fresh water, and the air we breathe。</p>\n<p>森林为我们所有人提供了大量的资源,包括食物、木材、药材、淡水以及我们呼吸的空气。</p>\n<p>Without the trees, species can disappear, the natural water balance can become disrupted and the ecosystem that supports the human population can</p>\n<p>如果没有树木,物种可能会消失,自然水循环可能会受到破坏,支撑人类生存的生态系统可能会崩溃。</p>",
