      "title": "Melting Ice",
      "type": "FIB_R",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>At the end of the last ice age, the melting ice disrupted the ocean currents in the North Atlantic and <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"forwent\">forwent</option><option value=\"up\">up</option><option value=\"never\">never</option><option value=\"caused\">caused</option><option value=\"could\">could</option><option value=\"around\">around</option><option value=\"though\">though</option><option value=\"thorough\">thorough</option></select> a drop in temperature of almost 5 degrees. Even <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"forwent\">forwent</option><option value=\"up\">up</option><option value=\"never\">never</option><option value=\"caused\">caused</option><option value=\"could\">could</option><option value=\"around\">around</option><option value=\"though\">though</option><option value=\"thorough\">thorough</option></select> the rest of the planet was warming <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"forwent\">forwent</option><option value=\"up\">up</option><option value=\"never\">never</option><option value=\"caused\">caused</option><option value=\"could\">could</option><option value=\"around\">around</option><option value=\"though\">though</option><option value=\"thorough\">thorough</option></select> ,the North Atlantic region remained in a cold period for 1300 years. The same thing happened <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"forwent\">forwent</option><option value=\"up\">up</option><option value=\"never\">never</option><option value=\"caused\">caused</option><option value=\"could\">could</option><option value=\"around\">around</option><option value=\"though\">though</option><option value=\"thorough\">thorough</option></select> 8000 years ago, when the cooling lasted about a hundred years, and it <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"5\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"forwent\">forwent</option><option value=\"up\">up</option><option value=\"never\">never</option><option value=\"caused\">caused</option><option value=\"could\">could</option><option value=\"around\">around</option><option value=\"though\">though</option><option value=\"thorough\">thorough</option></select> happen again today. Even a short period of cooling in the North Atlantic could have a dramatic effect on the wildlife, and the human populations, living there.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、caused</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“disrupted the ocean currents... and ______ a drop in temperature”，cause a drop in temperature 是常见搭配，意为“导致温度下降”。表示融冰扰乱了洋流并导致温度下降了近5度。因此填 caused。</p>\n<p>2、though</p>\n<p>考点:逻辑衔接</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“Even ______ the rest of the planet was warming...”，Even though 是固定搭配，意为“尽管/即使”，引导让步状语从句。表示尽管地球其他地区正在变暖，但北大西洋地区仍然保持了1300年的寒冷期。因此填 though。</p>\n<p>3、up</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“warming ______”，warm up 是固定搭配，意为“变暖”。表示地球其他地区正在变暖。因此填 up。</p>\n<p>4、around</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“happened ______ 8000 years ago”，around 8000 years ago 是常见表达，意为“大约8000年前”。表示大约8000年前同样的事情发生了。因此填 around。</p>\n<p>5、could</p>\n<p>考点:语法结构</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“and it ______ happen again today”，此处表示可能性。could 表示“可能”，符合语境，意为今天同样的事情“可能”再次发生。因此填 could。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>At the end of the last ice age, the melting ice disrupted the ocean currents in the North Atlantic and caused a drop in temperature of almost 5 degrees.</p>\n<p>在上一个冰河时代结束时,融化的冰破坏了北大西洋的洋流,导致气温下降了近5摄氏度。</p>\n<p>Even though the rest of the planet was warming up, the North Atlantic region remained in a cold period for 1300 years.</p>\n<p>即使尽管地球其他地区正在逐渐升温,北大西洋地区仍然经历了长达1300年的寒冷期。</p>\n<p>The same thing happened around 8000 years ago, when the cooling lasted</p>\n<p>同样的情况在大约8000年前也曾发生过,当时的降温持续了大约一百年,而这种情况今天可能再次发生。</p>\n<p>about a hundred years, and it could happen again today.</p>\n<p>即使在北大西洋地区短暂的降温也可能对当地野生动物和人类群体产生巨大的影</p>\n<p>Even a short period of cooling in the North Atlantic could have a dramatic effect on the wildlife, and the human populations, living there.</p>\n<p>响。</p>",
