      "passage_html": "<p>It is important to <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"level\">level</option><option value=\"gratification\">gratification</option><option value=\"emphasize\">emphasize</option><option value=\"taste\">taste</option><option value=\"prefer\">prefer</option><option value=\"expenditure\">expenditure</option><option value=\"laborious\">laborious</option><option value=\"expensive\">expensive</option><option value=\"meet\">meet</option></select> the need for hard work as an essential part of studying law, because far too many students are tempted to think that they can succeed by relying on what they imagine to be their natural ability, without bothering to add the <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"level\">level</option><option value=\"gratification\">gratification</option><option value=\"emphasize\">emphasize</option><option value=\"taste\">taste</option><option value=\"prefer\">prefer</option><option value=\"expenditure\">expenditure</option><option value=\"laborious\">laborious</option><option value=\"expensive\">expensive</option><option value=\"meet\">meet</option></select> of effort. To take an analogy some people prefer the more or less instant <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"level\">level</option><option value=\"gratification\">gratification</option><option value=\"emphasize\">emphasize</option><option value=\"taste\">taste</option><option value=\"prefer\">prefer</option><option value=\"expenditure\">expenditure</option><option value=\"laborious\">laborious</option><option value=\"expensive\">expensive</option><option value=\"meet\">meet</option></select> which comes from watching television adaptation of a classic novel to the rather more <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"level\">level</option><option value=\"gratification\">gratification</option><option value=\"emphasize\">emphasize</option><option value=\"taste\">taste</option><option value=\"prefer\">prefer</option><option value=\"expenditure\">expenditure</option><option value=\"laborious\">laborious</option><option value=\"expensive\">expensive</option><option value=\"meet\">meet</option></select> process of reading the novel itself. Those who <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"5\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"level\">level</option><option value=\"gratification\">gratification</option><option value=\"emphasize\">emphasize</option><option value=\"taste\">taste</option><option value=\"prefer\">prefer</option><option value=\"expenditure\">expenditure</option><option value=\"laborious\">laborious</option><option value=\"expensive\">expensive</option><option value=\"meet\">meet</option></select> watching television to reading the book are less likely to study law successfully, unless they rapidly acquire a <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"6\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"level\">level</option><option value=\"gratification\">gratification</option><option value=\"emphasize\">emphasize</option><option value=\"taste\">taste</option><option value=\"prefer\">prefer</option><option value=\"expenditure\">expenditure</option><option value=\"laborious\">laborious</option><option value=\"expensive\">expensive</option><option value=\"meet\">meet</option></select> for text-based materials .</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、emphasize</p>\n<p>考点:单句理解</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“It is important to ______ the need for hard work”，emphasize the need for sth. 是常见搭配，意为“强调对某事物的需求”。表示强调努力学习是学习法律的必要组成部分。因此填 emphasize。</p>\n<p>2、expenditure</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“adding the ______ of effort”，expenditure of effort 是常见搭配，意为“努力的付出”。表示许多学生自以为可以靠天赋成功，而不愿意付出努力。因此填 expenditure。</p>\n<p>3、gratification</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“instant ______”，instant gratification 是常见搭配，意为“即时的满足”。表示有些人更喜欢看电视改编经典小说所带来的即时满足感。因此填 gratification。</p>\n<p>4、laborious</p>\n<p>考点:上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“the rather more ______ process of reading the novel itself”。前文将看电视（即时满足）与读小说进行对比，读小说是一个更加“费力的/艰苦的”过程。laborious 意为“费力的”，与 instant gratification 形成对比。因此填 laborious。</p>\n<p>5、prefer</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“Those who ______ watching television to reading the book”，prefer A to B 是固定搭配，意为“喜欢A胜过B”。表示那些喜欢看电视胜过读书的人不太可能成功学习法律。因此填 prefer。</p>\n<p>6、taste</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“acquire a ______ for text-based materials”，acquire a taste for sth. 是固定搭配，意为“养成对某事物的爱好/逐渐喜欢上某事物”。表示除非他们迅速养成对文本材料的爱好。因此填 taste。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>It is important to emphasize the need for hard work as an essential part of studying law.</p>\n<p>以下是将中英文对照的内容:强调刻苦学习的重要性,将其作为学习法律的本质部分。</p>\n<p>Because far too many students are tempted to think that they can succeed by relying on what they imagine to be their natural ability, without bothering to add the expenditure of effort.</p>\n<p>因为太多学生诱惑于依靠自己想象的天赋来成功,却不乐意付出努力。</p>\n<p>To take an analogy, some people prefer the more or less instant gratification which comes from watching television adaptation of a classic novel to the rather more laborious process of reading the novel itself.</p>\n<p>举个例子,有些人更喜欢看经典小说改编的电视,相对于阅读小说本身这一更加费力的过程,他们更想要获得即时的满足。</p>\n<p>Those who prefer watching television to reading the book are less likely to study law successfully, unless they rapidly acquire a taste for text-based materials.</p>\n<p>那些更喜欢看电视而不是读书的人,学习法律成功的可能性较小,除非他们迅速获得对文本材料的感觉。</p>",
