      "title": "Giant Exoplanets",
      "type": "FIB_R",
      "frequency": "高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Giant exoplanets, like the so-called 'hot Jupiters' that are similar in <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"characteristics\">characteristics</option><option value=\"imagine\">imagine</option><option value=\"astronomers\">astronomers</option><option value=\"pilots\">pilots</option><option value=\"detect\">detect</option><option value=\"weight\">weight</option><option value=\"planet\">planet</option></select> to the solar system's biggest <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"characteristics\">characteristics</option><option value=\"imagine\">imagine</option><option value=\"astronomers\">astronomers</option><option value=\"pilots\">pilots</option><option value=\"detect\">detect</option><option value=\"weight\">weight</option><option value=\"planet\">planet</option></select> and orbit very close to their host stars, are excellent targets for <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"characteristics\">characteristics</option><option value=\"imagine\">imagine</option><option value=\"astronomers\">astronomers</option><option value=\"pilots\">pilots</option><option value=\"detect\">detect</option><option value=\"weight\">weight</option><option value=\"planet\">planet</option></select> in their search for their extrasolar worlds. The size and proximity of these planets is easy to <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"characteristics\">characteristics</option><option value=\"imagine\">imagine</option><option value=\"astronomers\">astronomers</option><option value=\"pilots\">pilots</option><option value=\"detect\">detect</option><option value=\"weight\">weight</option><option value=\"planet\">planet</option></select> as they create a large decrease in brightness when passing in front of their parent stars.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、characteristics</p>\n<p>考点:单句理解</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“similar in ______ to”。本句内部语义完整：热木星在“特征”上与太阳系最大的行星相似。仅凭本句即可判断需要表示“特征/特性”的名词。因此填 characteristics。</p>\n<p>2、planet</p>\n<p>考点:上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“the solar system‘s biggest ______”，太阳系中最大的“行星”是木星，planet 意为“行星”，符合语义。因此填 planet。</p>\n<p>3、astronomers</p>\n<p>考点:上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“excellent targets for ______ in their search”，寻找系外行星的应该是“天文学家”。因此填 astronomers。</p>\n<p>4、detect</p>\n<p>考点:单句理解</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“is easy to ______”。本句内部语义完整：这些行星的大小和接近程度很容易被“探测到”。因此填 detect。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Giant exoplanets, like the so-called 'hot Jupiters' that are similar in</p>\n<p>巨型系外行星,比如所谓的“热木星”,在特征上类似于太阳系最大的行星,并且它们的轨道非常接近其母星,是天文学家在寻找系外世界时的绝佳目标。</p>\n<p>characteristics to the solar system's biggest planet and orbit very close to their host stars, are excellent targets for astronomers in their search for their extrasolar worlds.</p>\n<p>这些行星的大小和近距离易于探测,因为它们在经过其母星前面时会造成亮度的</p>\n<p>The size and proximity of these planets is easy to detect as they create a large decrease in brightness when passing in front of their parent stars.</p>\n<p>大幅下降。</p>",
