      "question_id": 485,
      "title": "Seminars",
      "type": "FIB_R",
      "frequency": "高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Seminars are not designed to be mini-lectures. Their educational <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"part\">part</option><option value=\"provoke\">provoke</option><option value=\"unlikely\">unlikely</option><option value=\"job\">job</option><option value=\"theory\">theory</option><option value=\"service\">service</option><option value=\"role\">role</option><option value=\"assumption\">assumption</option><option value=\"impossible\">impossible</option><option value=\"stir\">stir</option></select> is to provide an opportunity for you to discuss interesting and difficult aspects of the course. This is founded on the <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"part\">part</option><option value=\"provoke\">provoke</option><option value=\"unlikely\">unlikely</option><option value=\"job\">job</option><option value=\"theory\">theory</option><option value=\"service\">service</option><option value=\"role\">role</option><option value=\"assumption\">assumption</option><option value=\"impossible\">impossible</option><option value=\"stir\">stir</option></select> that it is only by actively trying to use the knowledge that you have acquired from lectures and texts that you can achieve an adequate understanding of the subject. If you do not understand a point, it is highly <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"part\">part</option><option value=\"provoke\">provoke</option><option value=\"unlikely\">unlikely</option><option value=\"job\">job</option><option value=\"theory\">theory</option><option value=\"service\">service</option><option value=\"role\">role</option><option value=\"assumption\">assumption</option><option value=\"impossible\">impossible</option><option value=\"stir\">stir</option></select> that you will be the only person in the group in that position; you will invariably be undertaking a <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"part\">part</option><option value=\"provoke\">provoke</option><option value=\"unlikely\">unlikely</option><option value=\"job\">job</option><option value=\"theory\">theory</option><option value=\"service\">service</option><option value=\"role\">role</option><option value=\"assumption\">assumption</option><option value=\"impossible\">impossible</option><option value=\"stir\">stir</option></select> for the entire group, if you come to the seminar equipped with questions on matters which you feel you did not fully understand. The seminar is to introduce and <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"5\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"part\">part</option><option value=\"provoke\">provoke</option><option value=\"unlikely\">unlikely</option><option value=\"job\">job</option><option value=\"theory\">theory</option><option value=\"service\">service</option><option value=\"role\">role</option><option value=\"assumption\">assumption</option><option value=\"impossible\">impossible</option><option value=\"stir\">stir</option></select> discussion.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、role</p>\n<p>考点:单句理解</p>\n<p>解析: 句子说研讨课不是小型讲座,它的教育作用是让学生讨论课程中有趣和困难的内容。educational role 表示“教育作用”,符合该句语境,因此填 `role`。</p>\n<p>2、assumption</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: `founded on the assumption that` 构成固定搭配,意思是“建立在......假设之上”。句子说明研讨课的设置建立在一个假设之上:学生只有主动运用课堂和文本中学到的知识,才能真正理解课程内容。因此填 `assumption`。</p>\n<p>3、unlikely</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: `highly unlikely that` 构成固定搭配,意思是“极不可能......”。句子说明如果你不理解某个知识点,你极不可能是小组里唯一有这个困惑的人。因此填 `unlikely`。</p>\n<p>4、service</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: `undertake a service for` 构成固定搭配,意思是“为......提供帮助/服务”。句子说明带着问题参加研讨课,其实是在为整个小组提供帮助。因此填 `service`。</p>\n<p>5、provoke</p>\n<p>考点:并列结构</p>\n<p>解析: 这里看并列关系:`... and/or provoke` 在词性和语义上保持一致。原句相关表达是“which you feel you did not fully understand. The seminar is to introduce and provoke discussion.”,填 `provoke` 后,并列结构完整。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Seminars are not designed to be mini-lectures.</p>\n<p>会议并非设计用来成为微型讲座。</p>\n<p>Their educational role is to provide an opportunity for you to discuss interesting and difficult aspects of the course.</p>\n<p>他们的教育职能是为你提供机会讨论课程的</p>\n<p>This is founded on the assumption that it is only by actively trying to use the</p>\n<p>有趣和困难的方面。</p>\n<p>knowledge that you have acquired from lectures and texts that you can achieve an adequate understanding of the subject.</p>\n<p>这是建立在这样一个假设之上的,即只有通过在讲座和文本中获得的知识,并积极地尝试加以运用,你才能对主题有充分的理解。</p>\n<p>If you do not understand a point, it is highly unlikely that you will be the only person in the group in that position; you will invariably be undertaking a service for the entire group, if you come to the seminar equipped with questions on matters which you feel you did not fully understand.</p>\n<p>如果你不理解某一点,那么你极有可能是小组中唯一不明白这一点的人,如果你带着关于你认为自己并未完全理解的问题参加研讨会,你无疑将为整个小组提供服务。</p>\n<p>The seminar is to introduce and provoke discussion.</p>\n<p>研讨会的目的是介绍和引发讨论。</p>",
