      "id": "fib-r-5may-medium-330",
      "question_id": 330,
      "title": "Private School",
      "type": "FIB_R",
      "frequency": "中频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Private schools in the UK are redoubling their marketing efforts to foreigners. Almost a third of the 68,000 boarding pupils at such schools <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"weigh\">weigh</option><option value=\"already\">already</option><option value=\"unwilling\">unwilling</option><option value=\"fuss\">fuss</option><option value=\"account\">account</option><option value=\"seldom\">seldom</option><option value=\"shift\">shift</option></select> come from overseas. But now, with many UK residents <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"weigh\">weigh</option><option value=\"already\">already</option><option value=\"unwilling\">unwilling</option><option value=\"fuss\">fuss</option><option value=\"account\">account</option><option value=\"seldom\">seldom</option><option value=\"shift\">shift</option></select> or unable to afford the fees and a cultural <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"weigh\">weigh</option><option value=\"already\">already</option><option value=\"unwilling\">unwilling</option><option value=\"fuss\">fuss</option><option value=\"account\">account</option><option value=\"seldom\">seldom</option><option value=\"shift\">shift</option></select> away from boarding, many schools are looking abroad to survive. Overseas students now <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"weigh\">weigh</option><option value=\"already\">already</option><option value=\"unwilling\">unwilling</option><option value=\"fuss\">fuss</option><option value=\"account\">account</option><option value=\"seldom\">seldom</option><option value=\"shift\">shift</option></select> for about 500m pounds of fee income a year for boarding schools in the UK.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、already</p>\n<p>考点:上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“Almost a third of the 68,000 boarding pupils at such schools ______ come from overseas”。前一句提到英国私立学校正在加大对海外学生的营销力度，本句进一步说明现状：这类学校中近三分之一的学生“已经”来自海外。already 表示“已经”，强调这一趋势已经存在，与后文“now”形成时间上的呼应，说明在当前加大营销力度之前，海外生源已占相当比例。因此填 already。</p>\n<p>2、unwilling</p>\n<p>考点:并列结构</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“with many UK residents ______ or unable to afford the fees”。unwilling 和 unable 由 or 连接，构成并列结构，共同说明英国居民无法或不愿送孩子入读私立学校的原因。unwilling 意为“不愿意的”，与 unable（没能力的）形成语义上的并列，共同解释为什么学校要转向海外招生。因此填 unwilling。</p>\n<p>3、shift</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“a cultural ______ away from boarding”，cultural shift 是常见搭配，意为“文化转变/文化变迁”。表示英国社会出现了远离寄宿教育的文化转变，这也是学校转向海外招生的原因之一。因此填 shift。</p>\n<p>4、account</p>\n<p>考点:固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析: 空格位于“Overseas students now ______ for about 500m pounds of fee income”，account for 是固定搭配，在此处意为“占（比例/份额）”。表示海外学生现在每年为英国寄宿学校贡献约5亿英镑的学费收入。因此填 account。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Private schools in the UK are redoubling their marketing efforts to foreigners.</p>\n<p>英国私立学校正在加倍努力向外国学生进行宣传。</p>\n<p>Almost a third of the 68,000 boarding pupils at such schools already come from overseas.</p>\n<p>这些学校中 68000 名寄宿学生里，已经有将近三分之一来自海外。</p>\n<p>But now, with many UK residents unwilling or unable to afford the fees and a cultural shift away from boarding, many schools are looking abroad to survive.</p>\n<p>但是现在，由于许多英国居民不愿意或无力承担学费，同时文化上也逐渐远离寄宿制，许多学校为了生存正在把目光投向海外。</p>\n<p>Overseas students now account for about 500m pounds of fee income a year for boarding schools in the UK.</p>\n<p>海外学生现在每年为英国寄宿学校带来约 5 亿英镑的学费收入。</p>",
