      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>The environmental impact of the global textile industry is hard to overstate. One-third of the water used worldwide is spent fashioning fabrics. For every ton of cloth <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"produced\">produced</option><option value=\"produce\">produce</option><option value=\"producing\">producing</option><option value=\"is produced\">is produced</option></select> , 200 tons of water is polluted with chemicals and heavy metals. An estimated 1 trillion kilowatt-hours of electricity powers the factories that card and comb, spin and weave, and cut and stitch materials into everything from T-shirts to towels, <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"leave\">leave</option><option value=\"leaving\">leaving</option><option value=\"leaved\">leaved</option><option value=\"leaves\">leaves</option></select> behind mountains of solid waste and a massive carbon footprint. 'Where the industry is today is not really sustainable for the long term,' says Shreyaskar Chaudhary, chief executive of Pratibha Syntex, a textile manufacturer based outside Indore, India. With something of an 'if you build it, they will come' attitude, Mr.Chaudhary has steered Pratibha <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"around\">around</option><option value=\"among\">among</option><option value=\"toward\">toward</option><option value=\"through\">through</option></select> the leading edge of eco-friendly textile production. Under his direction, Pratibha began making clothes with organic cotton in 1999. Initially, the company couldn't find enough organic farms growing cotton in central India <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"have supplied\">have supplied</option><option value=\"supplying\">supplying</option><option value=\"to supply\">to supply</option><option value=\"is supplied\">is supplied</option></select> its factories. To meet production demands, Chaudhary's team had to convince conventional cotton farmers to change their growing methods.Pratibha provided seeds, cultivation instruction, and a guarantee of fair-trade prices for <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"5\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"their\">their</option><option value=\"its\">its</option><option value=\"mine\">mine</option><option value=\"them\">them</option></select> crops. Today, Pratibha has a network of 28,000 organic cotton growers across the central states of Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, and Orissa.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 produced</p>\n<p>考点：非谓语形式</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,空格处需要填入非谓语动词来修饰前面的名词 cloth(布料)。由于布料与动词 produce(生产)之间是被动关系,表示“被生产出来的布料”,因此需要使用过去分词形式 produced 作后置定语。因为此处是一个时间/条件状语结构(for every ton of cloth...),并没有完整的句子连接,所以不能直接使用谓语动词 is produced。</p>\n<p>2、 leaving</p>\n<p>考点：非谓语形式</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,前半句已经是一个结构完整的句子(An estimated 1 trillion... powers the factories...)。逗号后面的动词 leave 与前面主句的动作之间没有连词相连,因此不能使用谓语动词形式 leaves 或 leave。整个主句的工厂运作自然导致了后面的结果,属于自然发生的结果状语,因此使用现在分词形式 leaving 充当伴随或结果状语,在单句内部即可直接锁定。</p>\n<p>3、 toward</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：这个答案考查的是固定搭配。steer someone/something toward... 构成固定搭配,意思是“引导某人/某物走向......、朝着......的方向驶去”。在单句语境中,后文提到了“生态友好型纺织品生产的前沿(the leading edge of eco-friendly textile production)”,表示乔杜里先生正带领着公司“走向”这个积极环保的新方向,在单句内部即可锁定介词 toward。</p>\n<p>4、 to supply</p>\n<p>考点：非谓语形式</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,前面是完整的句子成分(the company couldn't find enough organic farms growing cotton in central India)。空格处需要填入一个非谓语动词来作目的状语,表示建立这些有机农场的“目的是为了”给他的工厂供应原材料。英语中通常使用动词不定式来表目的,因此锁定 to supply。</p>\n<p>5、 their</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,空格处需要一个代词来修饰后面的名词 crops(农作物)。根据前半句“乔杜里的团队不得不说服传统棉农(conventional cotton farmers)改变他们的种植方法”,可知后面 Pratibha 公司提供种子、指导并保证公平贸易价格的对象正是“这些农民的”农作物。主语为复数名词 farmers,对应的形容词性物主代词应当选择 their。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>The environmental impact of the global textile industry is hard to overstate.</p>\n<p>全球纺织业对环境的影响怎么夸大都不为过。</p>\n<p>One-third of the water used worldwide is spent fashioning fabrics.</p>\n<p>全球消耗的水资源中有三分之一被用于制作面料。</p>\n<p>For every ton of cloth produced, 200 tons of water is polluted with chemicals and heavy metals.</p>\n<p>每生产一吨布料,就有200吨水被化学物质和重金属污染。</p>\n<p>An estimated 1 trillion kilowatt-hours of electricity powers the factories that card and comb, spin and weave, and cut and stitch materials into everything from T-shirts to towels, leaving behind mountains of solid waste and a massive carbon footprint.</p>\n<p>据估计,有1万亿千瓦时的电力为那些将原材料经过梳理、纺纱、织布、裁剪和缝制成从T恤到毛巾等各种产品的工厂提供动力,从而留下了成堆的固体废物和巨大的碳足迹。</p>\n<p>'Where the industry is today is not really sustainable for the long term,' says Shreyaskar Chaudhary, chief executive of Pratibha Syntex, a textile manufacturer based outside Indore, India.</p>\n<p>总部位于印度印多尔市郊的纺织制造企业Pratibha Syntex的首席执行官什雷亚斯卡·乔杜里说:“该行业目前的现状在长期来看是不可持续的。”</p>\n<p>With something of an 'if you build it, they will come' attitude, Mr.Chaudhary has steered Pratibha toward the leading edge of eco-friendly textile production.</p>\n<p>怀着一种“只要你建好,人们总会来”的态度,乔杜里先生引导Pratibha公司走向了环保纺织品生产的最前沿。</p>\n<p>Under his direction, Pratibha began making clothes with organic cotton in 1999.</p>\n<p>在他的领导下,Pratibha于1999年开始用有机棉制作服装。</p>\n<p>Initially, the company couldn't find enough organic farms growing cotton in central India to supply its factories.</p>\n<p>最初,该公司在印度中部找不到足够的种植棉花的有机农场来供应其工厂。</p>\n<p>To meet production demands, Chaudhary's team had to convince conventional cotton farmers to change their growing methods.</p>\n<p>为了满足生产需求,乔杜里的团队不得不说服传统棉农改变他们的种植方法。</p>\n<p>Pratibha provided seeds, cultivation instruction, and a guarantee of fair-trade prices for their crops.</p>\n<p>Pratibha为他们提供种子、种植指导,并为他们的农作物提供公平贸易价格的保证。</p>\n<p>Today, Pratibha has a network of 28,000 organic cotton growers across the central states of Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, and Orissa.</p>\n<p>如今,Pratibha在中央邦、马哈拉施特拉邦和奥里萨邦等中部各邦拥有一个由28,000名有机棉种植者组成网络。</p>",
