      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Barrie Finning's, a professor at Monash University's college of pharmacy in Melbourne, and PhD student Anita Schneider, recently tested a new wrinkle cure. Twice daily, 20 male and female volunteers applied a liquid containing Myoxinol, a patented <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"example\">example</option><option value=\"exertion\">exertion</option><option value=\"explanation\">explanation</option><option value=\"extract\">extract</option></select> of okra (Hibiscus esculentus) seed, to one side of their faces. On the other side they applied a similar liquid without Myoxinol. Every week for a month their wrinkles were tested by self-assessment, photography and the size of depressions made in silicon moulds. The results were impressive. After a month the <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"concentration\">concentration</option><option value=\"depth\">depth</option><option value=\"prowess\">prowess</option><option value=\"strength\">strength</option></select> and number of wrinkles on the Myoxinol-treated side were reduced by approximately 27 per cent. But Finnin's research, commissioned by a cosmetics company, is unlikely to be published in a scientific <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"encyclopedia\">encyclopedia</option><option value=\"publicity\">publicity</option><option value=\"publication\">publication</option><option value=\"enclosure\">enclosure</option></select> . It's hard to even find studies that show the active ingredients in cosmetics penetrate the skin, let alone more comprehensive research on their effects. Even when <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"ritual\">ritual</option><option value=\"erratic\">erratic</option><option value=\"rough\">rough</option><option value=\"rigorous\">rigorous</option></select> studies are commissioned, companies usually control whether the work is published in the traditional scientific literature.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 extract</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,空格处需要一个名词来指代 Myoxinol 这种物质。括号内补充说明其成分是秋葵种子(okra seed),根据常识和化妆品研发语境,秋葵种子制成的护肤品活性成分应当是“提取物”。在选项中,example(例子)、exertion(努力、发挥)、explanation(解释)均不符合语境,只有 extract(提取物)最符合单句内部的语义搭配。</p>\n<p>2、 depth</p>\n<p>考点：上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析：单看这一句,wrinkles(皱纹)可以用多种维度衡量。但必须结合前文的跨句线索——前文提到研究人员通过“硅胶模具压痕的大小(the size of depressions made in silicon moulds)”来测试皱纹,模具压痕的大小对应的就是皱纹的“深度”。因此,选择 depth(深度)与前文的测试方法构成完美的上下文呼应。</p>\n<p>3、 publication</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：这个答案考查的是固定搭配。scientific publication 构成固定搭配,意思是“科学刊物、科学出版物”。在单句语境中,后文提到了“传统的科学文献(traditional scientific literature)”,与之呼应,前半句表达的是达尔文式的研究“不太可能在科学刊物上发表”,在单句内部即可直接锁定。</p>\n<p>4、 rigorous</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,空格处的形容词用来修饰名词 studies(研究)。前文提到“很难找到能证明化妆品活性成分渗透皮肤的研究,更不用说对其效果进行更全面的研究了”,后面用 Even when 进行了语气的转折和递进,表示“即使委托进行了‘严格的/严谨的’研究,公司通常也会控制这些成果是否发表”。在选项中,只有 rigorous(严格的、严谨的)符合科学实验的语境。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Barrie Finning's, a professor at Monash University's college of pharmacy in Melbourne, and PhD student Anita Schneider, recently tested a new wrinkle cure.</p>\n<p>墨尔本莫纳什大学药学院教授巴里·芬宁和博士生安妮塔·施耐德最近测试了一种新的去皱疗法。</p>\n<p>Twice daily, 20 male and female volunteers applied a liquid containing Myoxinol, a patented extract of okra (Hibiscus esculentus) seed, to one side of their faces.</p>\n<p>每天两次,20名男女志愿者将一种含有 Myoxinol(一种专利秋葵种子提取物)的液体涂抹在他们一侧的脸上。</p>\n<p>On the other side they applied a similar liquid without Myoxinol.</p>\n<p>在另一侧脸上,他们涂抹了一种不含 Myoxinol 的类似液体。</p>\n<p>Every week for a month their wrinkles were tested by self-assessment, photography and the size of depressions made in silicon moulds.</p>\n<p>在一个月的时间里,每周通过自我评估、拍照和测量硅胶模具压痕的大小来对他们的皱纹进行测试。</p>\n<p>The results were impressive.</p>\n<p>结果令人印象深刻。</p>\n<p>After a month the depth and number of wrinkles on the Myoxinol-treated side were reduced by approximately 27 per cent.</p>\n<p>一个月后,涂抹了 Myoxinol 一侧的皱纹深度和数量减少了大约27%。</p>\n<p>But Finnin's research, commissioned by a cosmetics company, is unlikely to be published in a scientific publication.</p>\n<p>但芬宁由一家化妆品公司资助的研究,不太可能在科学刊物上发表。</p>\n<p>It's hard to even find studies that show the active ingredients in cosmetics penetrate the skin, let alone more comprehensive research on their effects.</p>\n<p>甚至很难找到能证明化妆品中活性成分可以渗透皮肤的研究,更不用说对其效果进行更全面的研究了。</p>\n<p>Even when rigorous studies are commissioned, companies usually control whether the work is published in the traditional scientific literature.</p>\n<p>即使委托进行了严格的研究,公司通常也会控制该成果是否在传统的科学文献中发表。</p>",
