      "title": "Bones",
      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Bones are extremely strong. One of their <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"major\">major</option><option value=\"main\">main</option><option value=\"auxiliary\">auxiliary</option><option value=\"nominal\">nominal</option></select> functions is to protect organs. For example, the skull protects the brain; ribs protect <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"a\">a</option><option value=\"the\">the</option><option value=\"these\">these</option><option value=\"their\">their</option></select> heart and lungs. There are <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"two\">two</option><option value=\"four\">four</option><option value=\"five\">five</option><option value=\"three\">three</option></select> types of joints, including fixed joints, slightly moveable joints, and freely moving joints.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 main</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,空格处填入的形容词用来修饰 functions(功能)。骨骼有很多功能,而“保护器官”是其最核心、最基本的功能之一。虽然 main(主要的)和 major(主要的)在很多时候可以互换,但在描述事物“最根本、最基础的核心功能”时,习惯上更常使用 main function 这一固定表达。</p>\n<p>2、 the</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：这个答案考查的是定冠词的特指用法。在英语中,谈论人体特有的解剖学器官(如脑、心脏、肺等)时,通常需要使用定冠词 the 来表示独一无二的身体器官。前半句的“the skull protects the brain”已经给出了完美的句式示范,因此后半句并列的器官也应当使用相同的结构,即“ribs protect the heart and lungs”。</p>\n<p>3、 three</p>\n<p>考点：上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析：单看前半句无法直接锁定数字。但必须结合后文紧接着的跨句线索——后文用 including(包括)列举了具体类型:“固定关节(fixed joints)、微动关节(slightly moveable joints)以及活动关节(freely moving joints)”。后文清清楚楚地并列列举了三种类型,因此前面对应的数量必然是 three(三种)。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Bones are extremely strong.</p>\n<p>骨骼极其强壮。</p>\n<p>One of their main functions is to protect organs.</p>\n<p>它们的主要功能之一就是保护器官。</p>\n<p>For example, the skull protects the brain; ribs protect the heart and lungs.</p>\n<p>例如,颅骨保护大脑;肋骨保护心脏和肺部。</p>\n<p>There are three types of joints, including fixed joints, slightly moveable joints, and freely moving joints.</p>\n<p>关节共有三种类型,包括固定关节、微动关节和活动关节。</p>",
