      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Some students say that they need complete quiet to read and study. Others study best in a crowded, noisy room because the noise actually <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"helps\">helps</option><option value=\"hinders\">hinders</option><option value=\"aids\">aids</option><option value=\"assists\">assists</option></select> them concentrate. Some students like quiet music playing; others <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"prefer\">prefer</option><option value=\"perform\">perform</option><option value=\"do\">do</option><option value=\"complete\">complete</option></select> not. The point is, you should know the level of noise that is optimal for your own studying. However, one general rule for all students is that the television seems to be more of a distraction than music or other background noise, so <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"cut\">cut</option><option value=\"keep\">keep</option><option value=\"leave\">leave</option><option value=\"place\">place</option></select> the TV off when you are reading or studying. <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"Therefore\">Therefore</option><option value=\"However\">However</option><option value=\"Although\">Although</option><option value=\"Also\">Also</option></select> , don't let yourself become distracted by computer games, email, or Internet surfing.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 helps</p>\n<p>考点：上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析：单看这一句无法直接确定动词。前半句提到“另一些学生在拥挤、嘈杂的房间里学习效果最好”,后面用 because(因为)引导原因状语从句。既然他们能在嘈杂环境中“学得最好”,那必然是因为这种噪音在他们看来非但没有干扰,反而“帮助(helps)”了他们集中注意力。在选项中,虽然 aids 和 assists 也有帮助的意思,但 help 后面可以接省略 to 的动词不定式(help sb do sth),而 aid 和 assist 通常不这样搭配,故在单句内部即可直接锁定 helps。</p>\n<p>2、 do</p>\n<p>考点：上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析：前句说 Some students like quiet music playing,本句用 others 对应,结构为 others ______ not。do not 用于替代前文提到的谓语动词 like,构成 others do not (like quiet music playing) 的省略结构。prefer not、perform not、complete not 均不符合英语语法习惯。</p>\n<p>3、 leave</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：leave the TV off 为固定搭配,意为“让电视保持关闭状态”。leave + 名词 + 形容词 表示“使......处于某种状态”。cut off(切断/中断)、keep off(避开/不靠近,如 keep off the grass)、place off(不搭配),均不符合。</p>\n<p>4、 Also</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,空格处的副词用来连接前后两句话。前一句话建议学生们在学习时关闭电视以防分心,这一句话接着提到“不要让自己被电脑游戏、邮件或上网冲浪所分心”。这两句话在语义上是并列、递进和补充的关系,因此选择表示“此外、而且”的 Also 最为合适。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Some students say that they need complete quiet to read and study.</p>\n<p>一些学生说,他们需要完全安静的环境才能阅读和学习。</p>\n<p>Others study best in a crowded, noisy room because the noise actually helps them concentrate. Some students like quiet music playing; others do not.</p>\n<p>其他人在拥挤嘈杂的房间里学习效果最好,因为噪音实际上帮助他们集中注意力。有些学生喜欢安静的音乐;其他人则不喜欢。</p>\n<p>The point is, you should know the level of noise that is optimal for your own studying.</p>\n<p>关键是,你应该了解最适合你自己学习的噪音水平。</p>\n<p>However, one general rule for all students is that the television seems to be more of a distraction than music or other background noise, so leave the TV off when you are reading or studying.</p>\n<p>然而,对所有学生来说,一条普遍的规律是,电视似乎比音乐或其他背景噪音更容易让人分心,所以当你在阅读或学习时,请保持电视关闭的状态。</p>\n<p>Also, don't let yourself become distracted by computer games, email, or Internet surfing.</p>\n<p>此外,不要让自己被电脑游戏、电子邮件或上网冲浪分散了注意力。</p>",
