      "title": "Ancient Superhighway",
      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Even after thousands of years exploring Earth, we're still uncovering new things like an ancient 'superhighway' in the Guatemalan rain forest. Hidden beneath a thick layer of vegetation, the <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"network\">network</option><option value=\"distance\">distance</option><option value=\"interface\">interface</option><option value=\"width\">width</option></select> of roads stretches over 150 miles and was most likely built by the Mayan empire some 2,000 years ago. The newly mapped roads are connected to the ruins of El Mirador (sometimes called the Kan Kingdom) in northern Guatemala. Archaeologists believe El Mirador <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"has founded\">has founded</option><option value=\"founded\">founded</option><option value=\"was founded\">was founded</option><option value=\"was found\">was found</option></select> around the 6th century BCE, and was at its most powerful around the early first century CE. At that time, it had a population of as many as a quarter of a million, a quarter the size of Rome itself at the time. It also has some of the largest pyramids in the world. It was the <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"volume\">volume</option><option value=\"heart\">heart</option><option value=\"column\">column</option><option value=\"facet\">facet</option></select> of the Mayan civilization, and naturally needed some major roadways. The roads of El Mirador have been known about since 1967, but scientists had no idea how extensive they were until now. The thick jungle obscured the remnants of the road, <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"makes\">makes</option><option value=\"making\">making</option><option value=\"make\">make</option><option value=\"made\">made</option></select> it difficult to see from the air.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 network</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：名词 network 与后方的介词短语 of roads 构成了高频固定搭配 a network of roads(公路网 / 道路网络)。它在单句中精准表达“隐藏在厚厚的植被层之下,这一道路网络延伸了150多英里”。</p>\n<p>2、 was founded</p>\n<p>考点：时态语态</p>\n<p>解析：动词 found(建立、奠基)在此处充当谓语。由于主语 El Mirador(埃尔米拉多,古代玛雅城邦遗址)与动词“建立”之间是被动关系(即城邦是在公元前6世纪【被建立】的),且交代的是遥远的过去历史,根据时态语态规则,强制锁定一般过去时的被动语态形式 was founded。</p>\n<p>3、 heart</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：名词 heart 与后方的介词短语 of the Mayan civilization 构成了高频地道固定搭配 the heart of...(......的心脏 / ......的中心 / ......的核心地带)。它在单句中精准表达“它是玛雅文明的核心中心,自然需要一些主要的躯干道路”。</p>\n<p>4、 making</p>\n<p>考点：非谓语形式</p>\n<p>解析：现在分词 making 在此充当非谓语形式,在句中作伴随状语,承接前方的整个句子,表示顺理成章带来的自然结果。前文提到“茂密的丛林掩盖了道路的遗迹”,这一客观事实自然而然地“【使得(making)】从空中很难看清它们”。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Even after thousands of years exploring Earth, we're still uncovering new things like an ancient 'superhighway' in the Guatemalan rain forest.</p>\n<p>即使在探索地球数千年之后,我们仍然在发现新的事物,例如危地⻢拉雨林中的 一条古代“超级公路”。</p>\n<p>Hidden beneath a thick layer of vegetation, the network of roads stretches over 150 miles and was most likely built by the Mayan empire some 2,000 years ago.</p>\n<p>隐藏在厚厚的植被之下,这条道路网络绵延超过150英里,很可能是约2000年前 由玛雅帝国建造的。</p>\n<p>The newly mapped roads are connected to the ruins of El Mirador (sometimes called the Kan Kingdom) in northern Guatemala.</p>\n<p>这些新绘制的道路与位于危地⻢拉北部的埃尔米拉多遗址(有时被称为坎王国) 相连。</p>\n<p>Archaeologists believe El Mirador was founded around the 6th century BCE, and was at its most powerful around the early first century CE.</p>\n<p>考古学家认为,埃尔米拉多大约建于公元前6世纪,并在公元1世纪初达到最强盛 时期。</p>\n<p>At that time, it had a population of as many as a quarter of a million, a quarter the size of Rome itself at the time.</p>\n<p>当时,该城市人口多达25万,相当于当时罗⻢人口的四分之一。</p>\n<p>It also has some of the largest pyramids in the world.</p>\n<p>It was the heart of the Mayan civilization, and naturally needed some major roadways.</p>\n<p>它是玛雅文明的核心,自然需要一些主要的道路。</p>\n<p>The roads of El Mirador have been known about since 1967, but scientists had no idea how extensive they were until now.</p>\n<p>The thick jungle obscured the remnants of the road, making it difficult to see from the air.</p>\n<p>埃尔米拉多的道路早在1967年就已为人所知,但科学家们直到现在才意识到它们的规模有多么庞大。</p>\n<p>The thick jungle obscured the remnants of the road, making it difficult to see from the air。</p>\n<p>茂密的丛林遮蔽了道路遗迹,使其从空中难以看到。</p>",
