      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>A DOG may be man's best friend. But man is not always a dog's. Over the centuries <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"sequential\">sequential</option><option value=\"excessive\">excessive</option><option value=\"selective\">selective</option><option value=\"genetic\">genetic</option></select> breeding has pulled at the canine body shape to produce what is often a grotesque distortion of the underlying wolf. Indeed, some of these distortions are, when found in people, regarded as <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"dismissed\">dismissed</option><option value=\"disabled\">disabled</option><option value=\"pathologies\">pathologies</option><option value=\"diseases\">diseases</option></select> . Dog breeding does, though, offer a chance to those who would like to understand how body shape is controlled. The ancestry of pedigree pooches is well recorded, their generation time is short and their <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"little\">little</option><option value=\"offspring\">offspring</option><option value=\"puppy\">puppy</option><option value=\"litter\">litter</option></select> size reasonably large, so there is plenty of material to work with. <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"Hence\">Hence</option><option value=\"Moreover\">Moreover</option><option value=\"Although\">Although</option><option value=\"However\">However</option></select> ,breeds are, by definition, inbred, and this simplifies genetic analysis. Those such as Elaine Ostrander, of America's National Human Genome Research Institute, who wish to identify the genetic basis of the features of particular pedigrees thus have an <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"5\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"expected\">expected</option><option value=\"unusual\">unusual</option><option value=\"optimal\">optimal</option><option value=\"ideal\">ideal</option></select> experimental animal.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 selective</p>\n<p>考点：上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析：形容词 selective(选择性的)在此处描述育种方式。单句逻辑指人类通过“【选择性】”育种来塑造犬只体型,最终产生远超原始狼类特征的变异。</p>\n<p>2、 pathologies</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：名词 pathologies(病理状态)在此处与人类的生理失调对比。文中指出狗身上的一些体型扭曲,若出现在人类身上,会被视为某种“【病理状态】”。</p>\n<p>3、 litter</p>\n<p>考点：上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析：名词 litter(一窝幼崽)在此处指代繁殖数量。犬只繁殖的特点是“【一窝】”数量较大,这为研究提供了丰富的实验素材。</p>\n<p>4、 Moreover</p>\n<p>考点：逻辑衔接</p>\n<p>解析：副词 Moreover(此外 / 而且)在此处起到递进逻辑的作用。前文提到了研究犬只的优势,此处进一步递进说明“【此外】”,品种本身就是近亲繁殖的,这进一步简化了遗传分析。</p>\n<p>5、 ideal</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：形容词 ideal(理想的)在此处描述实验动物。因为品种特征明确且易于分析,所以对于 Elaine Ostrander 等研究人员来说,这是一种“【理想的】”实验动物。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>A DOG may be man's best friend.</p>\n<p>一只狗可能是人类最好的朋友。 But man is not always a dog's.</p>\n<p>但人类并不总是狗的。</p>\n<p>But man is not always a dog's.</p>\n<p>几个世纪以来,选择性育种拉扯犬类体型,产生了往往是狼基础的令人扭曲的变种。</p>\n<p>Over the centuries selective breeding has pulled at the canine body shape to produce what is often a grotesque distortion of the underlying wolf.</p>\n<p>事实上,当这些扭曲出现在人类身上时,就会被视为病态。</p>\n<p>Indeed, some of these distortions are, when found in people, regarded as pathologies .</p>\n<p>不过,狗育种确实为那些想了解体型如何控制的人提供了机会。</p>\n<p>Dog breeding does, though, offer a chance to those who would like to understand how body shape is controlled.</p>\n<p>系谱犬的祖先记录良好,它们的繁殖期短,窝产仔数相当大,所以有大量的材料 可以研究。</p>\n<p>The ancestry of pedigree pooches is well recorded, their generation time is short and their litter size reasonably large, so there is plenty of material to work with.</p>\n<p>而且,品种狗,顾名思义,是近亲繁殖的,这简化了基因分析。</p>\n<p>Moreover ,breeds are, by definition, inbred, and this simplifies genetic analysis.</p>\n<p>美国国立人类基因组研究学院的伊莱恩·奥斯特兰德的理想实验动物,可以帮助 其确定特定系谱特征遗传基础。</p>\n<p>Those such as Elaine Ostrander, of America's National Human Genome Research Institute, who wish to identify the genetic basis of the features of particular pedigrees thus have an ideal experimental animal.</p>",
