      "title": "David Lynch",
      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>David Lynch is professor and head of education at Charles Darwin University. <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"After\">After</option><option value=\"Prior\">Prior</option><option value=\"Last\">Last</option><option value=\"Before\">Before</option></select> to this he was sub dean in the Faculty of Education and Creative Arts at Central Queensland University and foundation head of the University’s Noosa <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"campus\">campus</option><option value=\"place\">place</option><option value=\"camp\">camp</option><option value=\"college\">college</option></select> . David’s career in education began as a primary school teacher in Queensland in the early 1980’s and <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"projected\">projected</option><option value=\"processed\">processed</option><option value=\"pronounced\">pronounced</option><option value=\"progressed\">progressed</option></select> to four principal positions before <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"leaving\">leaving</option><option value=\"hiring\">hiring</option><option value=\"entering\">entering</option><option value=\"having\">having</option></select> higher education. David’s research interests predominate in teacher education with particular interest in building teacher capability to meet a changed world.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 Prior</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：介词短语 Prior to(在......之前)在学术传记中是非常正式的时间表达方式。整句逻辑表达他在担任现职“【之前】”,曾在其他大学任职。</p>\n<p>2、 campus</p>\n<p>考点：上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析：名词 campus(校区)与 university(大学)是配套的地理位置词汇。文中提到的 Noosa 是该大学的一个“【校区】”,这符合高等教育机构的组织架构描述。</p>\n<p>3、 progressed</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：动词 progress(进展 / 逐步发展)在此处描述职业生涯的晋升路径。从小学教师到担任四所学校的校长,这是一个职业阶梯的自然“【发展 / 进阶】”过程。</p>\n<p>4、 entering</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：动词 enter(进入)在此处指代职业生涯的转换。单句表达他在“【进入】”高等教育领域之前,已经担任过四所学校的校长职位。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>David Lynch is professor and head of education at Charles Darwin University.</p>\n<p>大卫·林奇是查尔斯·达尔文大学的教育学教授和教育学院院⻓。</p>\n<p>Prior to this he was sub dean in the Faculty of Education and Creative Arts at Central Queensland University and foundation head of the University’s Noosa campus .</p>\n<p>在此之前,他是中央昆士兰大学教育与创意艺术学院的主管,也是该大学努萨校 区的创始人。</p>\n<p>David’s career in education began as a primary school teacher in Queensland in the early 1980’s and progressed to four principal positions before entering higher education.</p>\n<p>大卫的教育事业始于20世纪80年代初在昆士兰当一名小学教师,在进入高等教 育领域之前,他担任过四所学校的校⻓。</p>\n<p>David’s research interests predominate in teacher education with particular interest in building teacher capability to meet a changed world.</p>\n<p>大卫的研究兴趣主要集中在教师教育方面,特别感兴趣的是培养教师适应不断变 化世界的能力。</p>",
