      "title": "Wilful Blindness",
      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Willful blindness had started life as a legal concept in the nineteenth century. A judge in Regina v. Sleep ruled that an accused could not be convicted for <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"robbery\">robbery</option><option value=\"possession\">possession</option><option value=\"registration\">registration</option><option value=\"inquisition\">inquisition</option></select> of government property unless the jury found that he either knew the goods came from government stores or had &quot;willfully shut his eyes to the fact&quot;. <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"Howbeit\">Howbeit</option><option value=\"Therefore\">Therefore</option><option value=\"Thereby\">Thereby</option><option value=\"Thereafter\">Thereafter</option></select> , English judicial authorities referred to the state of mind that accompanied one who &quot;willfully shut his eyes&quot; as &quot;connivance&quot; or &quot;constructive knowledge.&quot; Over time, lots of other phrases came into play — &quot;deliberate or willful ignorance&quot;, &quot;conscious avoidance&quot;, and &quot;deliberate indifference&quot;. What they all have in <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"contrast\">contrast</option><option value=\"total\">total</option><option value=\"relation\">relation</option><option value=\"common\">common</option></select> is the idea that there is an opportunity for knowledge and a responsibility to be informed, but it is shirked. Nowadays, the law is <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"little\">little</option><option value=\"few\">few</option><option value=\"most\">most</option><option value=\"less\">less</option></select> often applied in cases of money laundering and drug trafficking: if you've been paid a large amount of money to carry a suitcase, then you are being willfully blind if you don't check what is inside.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 possession</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：句中说被告不能因______政府财产而被定罪。possession(持有/拥有)符合法律语境,指持有政府财产。robbery(抢劫)、registration(登记)、inquisition(审讯/调查)均不符合。</p>\n<p>2、 thereafter</p>\n<p>考点：逻辑衔接</p>\n<p>解析：前文描述19世纪某案件中的裁定,后文说英国司法机构此后将某种心理状态称为“默许”或“推定知情”。thereafter(此后)表示时间上的承接关系。howbeit(尽管如此,古语)罕见且不符合;therefore(因此)表因果,但前后并非因果关系;thereby(借此)表方式或结果,不符合。</p>\n<p>3、 common</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：have in common 为固定搭配,意为“有共同之处”。have in contrast(对比之下有)、have in total(总计有)、have in relation(有关系)均不符合。</p>\n<p>4、 most</p>\n<p>考点：上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析：句中说如今该法律______常用于洗钱和贩毒案件。most often 为常见搭配,意为“最经常”。little(很少)与后文例子矛盾;few 修饰可数名词,不能修饰 often;less 是比较级,文中无比较对象。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Willful blindness had started life as a legal concept in the nineteenth century.</p>\n<p>故意忽视最初是19世纪的一个法律概念。</p>\n<p>A judge in Regina v. Sleep ruled that an accused could not be convicted for possession of government property unless the jury found that he either knew the goods came from government stores or had &quot;willfully shut his eyes to the fact&quot;.</p>\n<p>在“女王诉斯利普案”中,一名法官裁定,不能因持有政府财产而判定被告有罪,除非陪审团认定他要么知道货物来自政府仓库,要么“故意对事实视而不见”。</p>\n<p>Thereafter, English judicial authorities referred to the state of mind that accompanied one who &quot;willfully shut his eyes&quot; as &quot;connivance&quot; or &quot;constructive knowledge.&quot;</p>\n<p>此后,英国司法机构将伴随“故意视而不见”者的心理状态称为“默许”或“推定知情”。</p>\n<p>Over time, lots of other phrases came into play — &quot;deliberate or willful ignorance&quot;, &quot;conscious avoidance&quot;, and &quot;deliberate indifference&quot;.</p>\n<p>随着时间的推移,许多其他短语开始使用——“故意或蓄意忽视”、“有意识回避”和“故意漠不关心”。</p>\n<p>What they all have in common is the idea that there is an opportunity for knowledge and a responsibility to be informed, but it is shirked.</p>\n<p>它们的共同点是:存在获取知识的机会和被告知的责任,但这些被推卸了。</p>\n<p>Nowadays, the law is most often applied in cases of money laundering and drug trafficking: if you've been paid a large amount of money to carry a suitcase, then you are being willfully blind if you don't check what is inside.</p>\n<p>如今,该法律最常用于洗钱和贩毒案件:如果你被支付大量金钱去携带一个手提箱,却不检查里面有什么,那么你就是故意忽视。</p>",
