      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "极高频",
      "passage_html": "<p>In the UK, it is recommended that drivers should turn off their car engines when they expect to be stationary for more than 1 minute. To encourage drivers <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"to turn\">to turn</option><option value=\"turn\">turn</option><option value=\"turning\">turning</option><option value=\"turned\">turned</option></select> their engines while waiting at rail crossings, the Kent city council placed a permanent sign at the crossing asking drivers to &quot;please switch off your engine when barriers are down to help improve air quality.&quot; <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"instance\">instance</option><option value=\"average\">average</option><option value=\"addition\">addition</option><option value=\"commit\">commit</option></select> , drivers had to wait between 2 and 3 minutes to cross after the barrier had gone down. However, the sign didn't seem to be convincing the <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"exception\">exception</option><option value=\"most\">most</option><option value=\"majority\">majority</option><option value=\"unity\">unity</option></select> of drivers to switch off their engines. &quot; <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"Although\">Although</option><option value=\"Since\">Since</option><option value=\"Because\">Because</option><option value=\"However\">However</option></select> some research suggests that signs <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"5\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"alone\">alone</option><option value=\"lonely\">lonely</option><option value=\"neither\">neither</option><option value=\"either\">either</option></select> can change behavior, the message on this sign was designed simply to be an informational request and was not guided by any particular behavioral theory,&quot; the researchers explain. So the research team, led by Rose Mellady of the University of East Anglia, designed an intervention study.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 to turn</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：这个答案考查的是固定搭配。encourage someone to do something 构成固定搭配,意思是“鼓励某人做某事”。在单句语境中,主句动词为 placed(放置),此处使用动词不定式形式 to turn 作为名词词组后面的目的状语,用以明确该标志牌设立的核心意图。</p>\n<p>2、 average</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：这个答案考查的是固定搭配。on average 构成固定搭配,意思是“平均而言”。在单句语境中,虽然开头省略了介词 on,但在完形填空对特定短语的考查中,此处选择副词化名词 average 来修饰整句的时间区间(2 to 3 minutes),用以说明司机的平均等待时间。</p>\n<p>3、 majority</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：这个答案考查的是单句理解。通过对本句的成分进行分析,didn't seem to be convincing the majority of drivers 意为“似乎未能说服大多数司机”。the majority of 为常见表达,意为“大多数、绝大部分”,用来准确陈述大部分司机并未在看到标志后关闭发动机的客观事实。</p>\n<p>4、 Although</p>\n<p>考点：逻辑衔接</p>\n<p>解析：这个答案考查的是逻辑衔接。前半句提到“一些研究表明单靠标志牌就能改变人们的行为”,后半句转折指出“这个标志牌上的信息设计仅仅是一个告知性请求,并没有任何特定行为理论的指导”。前后两部分语义存在明显的让步与对比关系,因此使用 Although 引导让步状语从句。</p>\n<p>5、 alone</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：这个答案考查的是单句理解。在主语从句中,主语为 signs(标志牌),后置修饰词选择副词 alone,构成 signs alone 结构,意为“单靠标志牌、仅仅标志牌本身”,用以在单句内强调无其他干预手段、仅凭牌子这一个体改变行为的可能性。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>In the UK, it is recommended that drivers should turn off their car engines when they expect to be stationary for more than 1 minute.</p>\n<p>在英国,当驾驶员预计⻋辆将静止超过1分钟时,建议他们关掉汽⻋引擎。</p>\n<p>To encourage drivers to turn their engines while waiting at rail crossings, the Kent city council placed a permanent sign at the crossing asking drivers to &quot;please switch off your engine when barriers are down to help improve air quality.&quot; average , drivers had to wait between 2 and 3 minutes to cross after the barrier had gone down.</p>\n<p>为了鼓励驾驶员在等候火⻋通过时关掉引擎,肯特市议会曾在路口设置了一块永 久性的标语牌,要求驾驶员“当栅栏放下时,请关掉引擎以帮助改善空气质量。”</p>\n<p>However, the sign didn't seem to be convincing the majority of drivers to switch off their engines.</p>\n<p>平均而言,在栅栏放下之后,驾驶员们不得不等待2至3分钟才能通过。</p>\n<p>&quot; Although some research suggests that signs alone can change behavior, the message on this sign was designed simply to be an informational request and was not guided by any particular behavioral theory,&quot; the researchers explain.</p>\n<p>然而,这块标语牌似乎并没有说服大多数驾驶员关掉他们的引擎。</p>\n<p>So the research team, led by Rose Mellady of the University of East Anglia, designed an intervention study.</p>\n<p>是被设计为一个信息请求,并没有任何特定的行为理论作为指导,”研究者们解释 称。</p>\n<p>So the research team, led by Rose Mellady of the University of East Anglia, designed an intervention study.</p>\n<p>于是,由东英吉利大学的罗斯·梅拉迪领导的研究团队设计了一项干预研究。</p>",
