      "id": "fib-rw-5may-medium-136",
      "question_id": 136,
      "title": "Buying a House",
      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "中频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Buying a <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"house\">house</option><option value=\"architecture\">architecture</option><option value=\"structure\">structure</option><option value=\"family\">family</option></select> can seem like a daunting process. First you need to work out how much you can borrow. This is where our services will really help you. Make sure you have an accurate and detailed budget that takes into account all associated with purchasing a property, including stamp duty, council rates, and other fees. We can help you identify these extra costs. Ask us for our budget planner if you don't already have one. Interest rates move constantly, so you will need to allow room in your budget for interest rate increases and for other <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"unbelievable\">unbelievable</option><option value=\"unforgettable\">unforgettable</option><option value=\"unforeseen\">unforeseen</option><option value=\"certain\">certain</option></select> events. All purchase funds are paid at settlement. In the <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"normal events\">normal events</option><option value=\"uncertain course\">uncertain course</option><option value=\"ordinary course\">ordinary course</option><option value=\"special course\">special course</option></select> of events, settlement takes place, the purchase price is paid in full and the deposit bond simply lapses into group certificates for the <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"mere\">mere</option><option value=\"leading\">leading</option><option value=\"next\">next</option><option value=\"past\">past</option></select> two years.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 house</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：Buying a house 固定搭配,意为“买房子、置业”。结合后文“计算你能借到多少钱”、“购买一处房产(purchasing a property)”等上下文线索,完美印证此处是指买房的过程。</p>\n<p>2、 unforeseen</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,形容词作定语修饰名词 events。结合前文“利率在不断变动,因此你必须在预算中留出空间”这一防范风险的语境可知,预留空间是为了应对利率上升或其他“无法预料的/突发的(unforeseen)”意外事件。</p>\n<p>3、 ordinary course</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：in the ordinary course of events 固定搭配,意为“在通常情况下/按照正常的事务程序”。在单句语境中,指代在正常交易程序下房产交割的顺利进行。</p>\n<p>4、 past</p>\n<p>考点：上下文语境</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,形容词作定语修饰数词短语 two years。结合全篇关于回顾买房交割完成、原本的定金债券随之在过去两年时间里转化为团体证书的叙事语境,填入“过去的(past)”以切合时间流逝。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Buying a house can seem like a daunting process.</p>\n<p>买房子似乎是一个令人望而生畏的过程。</p>\n<p>First you need to work out how much you can borrow. This is where our services will really help you.</p>\n<p>首先你需要计算出你能借多少钱。这正是我们的服务能真正帮到你的地方。</p>\n<p>Make sure you have an accurate and detailed budget that takes into account all associated with purchasing a property, including stamp duty, council rates, and other fees. We can help you identify these extra costs. Ask us for our budget planner if you don't already have one.</p>\n<p>确保你有一个准确而详细的预算,将与购买房产相关的所有费用都考虑在内,包括印花税、市政税和其他费用。我们可以帮你识别这些额外的成本。如果你还没有我们的预算规划师,请向我们索取。</p>\n<p>Interest rates move constantly, so you will need to allow room in your budget for interest rate increases and for other unforeseen events.</p>\n<p>利率在不断变化,因此你需要在预算中留出空间,以应对利率上升和其他不可预见的事件。</p>\n<p>All purchase funds are paid at settlement.</p>\n<p>所有的购买资金都在交割时支付。</p>\n<p>In the ordinary course of events, settlement takes place, the purchase price is paid in full and the deposit bond simply lapses into group certificates for the past two years.</p>\n<p>在通常情况下,交割会顺利进行,购房款会全额支付,而过去两年的定金债券则直接转为团体证书。</p>",
