      "id": "fib-rw-5may-medium-581",
      "question_id": 581,
      "title": "Sales Activities",
      "type": "FIB_RW",
      "frequency": "中频",
      "passage_html": "<p>Organizations need to integrate their sales activities more both internally and with customers' needs according to a new book co- authored by an academic at the University of East Anglia. The book <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"1\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"predicts\">predicts</option><option value=\"informs\">informs</option><option value=\"addresses\">addresses</option><option value=\"writes\">writes</option></select> how sales can help organizations to become more customer-oriented and considers how they are responding to challenges such as increasing competition, more <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"2\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"demanding\">demanding</option><option value=\"aggressive\">aggressive</option><option value=\"friendly\">friendly</option><option value=\"needy\">needy</option></select> customers and a more complex selling environment. Many organizations are facing escalating costs and a growth in customer power, <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"3\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"which\">which</option><option value=\"this\">this</option><option value=\"that\">that</option><option value=\"where\">where</option></select> makes it necessary to allocate resources more strategically. The sales function can provide critical customer and market knowledge to help inform both innovation and marketing. However, the authors say that within the industry <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"4\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"that\">that</option><option value=\"there\">there</option><option value=\"which\">which</option><option value=\"it\">it</option></select> is still uncertainty about the shape a future sales team should take, how it should be managed, and how it <select class=\"blank-select\" data-blank-index=\"5\"><option value=\"\">选择答案</option><option value=\"applies\">applies</option><option value=\"suits\">suits</option><option value=\"fits\">fits</option><option value=\"matches\">matches</option></select> into their organization's business model.</p>",
      "analysis_html": "<p>1、 addresses</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,动词充当主句谓语。主语是 `The book`(这本书),宾语是由 `how` 引导的从句。单句字面逻辑在阐述这本书的核心内容,表示这本书“【探讨/论述(addresses)】”了销售如何帮助组织变得更加以客户为导向。其他干扰项(如预测、通知)不符合该学术书籍的论述属性。</p>\n<p>2、 demanding</p>\n<p>考点：单句理解</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,形容词作定语修饰名词 `customers`(客户)。它与前方的名词 `competition`(日益激烈的竞争)处于同一个应对挑战的递进线索中。在四个选项中,只有 demanding(苛求的、高要求的)符合现代市场营销学中企业所面临的“越来越【挑剔/高要求】的客户”这一字面逻辑。</p>\n<p>3、 which</p>\n<p>考点：定语从句</p>\n<p>解析：在单句语境中,关系代词 which 在此引导一个非限制性定语从句,并在从句中充当主语。它的指代对象是前方的整个主句事实(许多组织面临成本上升和客户权力增长),在语义上精准表达“【这一情况】使得更有策略地分配资源变得极其必要”。</p>\n<p>4、 there</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：在由 `that` 引导的宾语从句中,代词 there 与后方的系动词 `is` 构成了英语中最核心的固定搭配 `there is`(存在...... / 有......)。它在单句中用来极其规范地引出从句的实际主语 `uncertainty`(不确定性)。</p>\n<p>5、 fits</p>\n<p>考点：固定搭配</p>\n<p>解析：动词 fits 与后方的介词 `into` 构成了固定搭配 `fit into`(融入...... / 适合......)。它在单句中充当并列从句的谓语核心,精准表达了销售团队未来应当“如何【融入】其组织的商业模式”这一管理学命题。</p>",
      "translation_html": "<p>Organizations need to integrate their sales activities more both internally and with customers' needs according to a new book co- authored by an academic at the University of East Anglia.</p>\n<p>根据东英吉利大学一位学者合著的一本新书,企业需要将他们的销售活动在内部以及与客户需求之间进行更紧密的整合。</p>\n<p>The book addresses how sales can help organizations to become more customer-oriented and considers how they are responding to challenges such as increasing competition, more demanding customers and a more complex selling environment.</p>\n<p>该书探讨了销售如何帮助企业变得更加以客户为导向,并思考了它们如何应对诸如日益激烈的竞争、要求更高的客户以及更复杂的销售环境等挑战。</p>\n<p>Many organizations are facing escalating costs and a growth in customer power, which makes it necessary to allocate resources more strategically.</p>\n<p>许多组织正面临着不断攀升的成本和客户权力的增长,这使得更有策略地分配资源变得极其必要。</p>\n<p>The sales function can provide critical customer and market knowledge to help inform both innovation and marketing.</p>\n<p>销售职能可以提供关键的客户和市场知识,以帮助隐喻和指导创新与营销。</p>\n<p>However, the authors say that within the industry there is still uncertainty about the shape a future sales team should take, how it should be managed, and how it fits into their organization's business model.</p>\n<p>然而,作者表示,在行业内部,关于未来销售团队应当采取的形式、应当如何管理以及它如何融入其企业的商业模式,依然存在着不确定性。</p>",
